WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:04.220
Cinnamon. Cordial is a
distilled spirit that is

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.140
both sweet and spicy.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.990
It's this complexity of
flavor that is at the

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.400
heart of its appeal.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.330
This particular cinnamon
cordial starts with a

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.090
blend of California
grape brandy that's been

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:18.830
aged two years.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:21.770
The distiller measures
the amount, the recipe

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.590
calls for and pours it
into the main production

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:28.790
vessel. He then pumps
neutral grain spirits out

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.220
of a big holding tank
and into the measuring

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:36.050
bucket. This spirit is
190 proof, which means

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.360
that it's 95% alcohol.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.510
He adds it to the grape
brandy.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.590
Together, the brandy and
the neutral spirits will

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.840
serve as the alcohol
base for the cinnamon

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.380
cordial. The brandy
contributes color and a

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.440
little flavor, while the
clear spirits add

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.310
potency.

